{"study_accession":"PRJNA827794","secondary_study_accession":"SRP370865","title":"A distinct immature low-density neutrophil population characterizes acute generalized pustular psoriasis [PBMC]","description":"Generalized pustular psoriasis (GPP) is a severe disease featured by neutrophilic pustules and enhanced IL-36 inflammatory pathway in skin. Recently, a transcriptomic analysis of PBMCs and neutrophils in MPO-deficient GPP patients has been performed in stable disease state. However, transcriptomic profiling of PBMCs during acute flare of GPP is unclear. Here, we reported a predominant neutrophil signature in GPP PBMC and a marked increase in the CD66+CD16+ low-density neutrophils (LDNs) within the PBMC fraction of acute GPP patients. Transcriptomic and functional analysis of LDNs revealed a hypoinflammatory phenotype yet enhanced release of neutrophil granule proteases, implicating that LDNs might contribute to the IL-36-mediated inflammation in GPP patients. Overall design: Comparative gene expression profiling analysis of RNA-seq data for peripheral blood mononulear cells (PBMCs) from 8 generalized pustular psoriasis (GPP) patients, 8 psoriasis vulgaris (PV) patients and 8 healthy donors.","pubmed":"35500640","geo_series":"","n_samples":24,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN27621216","study_accession":"PRJNA827794","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"PV8","description":"PV8","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM6047733","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2022-04-21","attributes":[["source_name","Blood"],["tissue","Blood"],["disease","Psoriasis vulgaris (PV)"],["cell_type","Peripheral blood mononuclear cell (PBMC)"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR18793048","experiment_accession":"SRX14891735","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"HiSeq X Ten","read_count":25048778,"base_count":7067878632,"first_public":"2022-04-21","experiment_title":"HiSeq X Ten sequencing: GSM6047733: PV8 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"la